oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome failure
file Makefile kept 9
| # The same chain without `-k`. GNU Make abandons the rest of the chain at the
| # first entry that fails, so only the first recipe's mark is in the log. This
| # is the half of the behaviour that says the chain edge is still an ordering:
| # the later entries are reachable, and what stops them is the run ending.
| out:: n1
| 	@printf '%s\n' first >> log
| 	@false
| out:: n2
| 	@printf '%s\n' second >> log
file log touched 1
| first
file n1 kept 1
| a
file n2 kept 1
| b
